## Surviving hole (H1, reported, NOT fixed)
"failed to reproduce" — the most idiomatic paraphrase of a denial of
reproduction — and "could not get it to fail" are still accepted as
observations. The filter remains an enumerated deny-list (contractions,
inability, "not <adj>", absence phrases, does/did-not-reproduce); any denial
phrased outside those classes counts as an observation. The stub exit 1 does
not distinguish this: the failure is only the standing NOT PERFORMED count.
Fairness: the check comment already defers semantic genuineness to the
independent verifier's read, and the fix materially narrows R1 (my three
recorded paraphrases are now caught). Closing the class fully would need a
positive-shaped observation requirement (e.g. command/exit/observed markers)
or a wider deny-list — the builder's call, not applied by QA.

